# Line-ending normalisation (matters when the repo moves between machines).
#
# Without this, Windows' default `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites every text file to
# CRLF on checkout, so a repo committed on Windows shows "modified" everywhere on
# macOS/Linux — and vice versa. Storing LF and checking out LF keeps the working
# tree identical on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell / batch scripts keep their native endings.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.sh  text eol=lf

# Explicitly binary: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.zip binary

# Generated / snapshot files where a diff is pure noise.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated
